```js
const list = document.querySelector("#todos");

list?.addEventListener("click", (event) => {
  const button = event.target.closest("button[data-action='delete']");
  if (!button || !list.contains(button)) return;   // click wasn't on a delete button.
  button.closest("li")?.remove();
});

// Later: new items need no new listeners.
const li = document.createElement("li");
li.textContent = "Walk the dog ";
const del = document.createElement("button");
del.dataset.action = "delete";
del.textContent = "Delete";
li.append(del);
list?.append(li);
```

| Call | Effect |
|---|---|
| `event.target`. | the innermost element clicked, e.g. a span inside the button. |
| `event.currentTarget`. | the element whose listener is running (the list). |
| `closest(selector)`. | walks up from target to the nearest match. |
| `preventDefault()`. | cancel the browser's default action only. |
| `stopPropagation()`. | stop travelling to further ancestors. |

